<overview>
<p>Mechanized tracked platoons move their infantry in armored personnel carriers fitted with tracks for reliable all-terrain performance. Tracked APCs handle mud, snow, rubble, and rough ground better than any wheeled or hover alternative, making these platoons the preferred mechanized infantry for operations where terrain is uncertain or hostile. They sacrifice road speed compared to wheeled formations but gain the ability to keep pace with armored vehicles across broken ground. The APCs provide meaningful ballistic protection during transit, though troops must still dismount to fight effectively.</p><p>Towing Arrow IV artillery systems, these platoons field the most sophisticated indirect fire capability available to conventional forces, launching guided missiles that can be directed onto targets by forward observers with TAG designators.</p>
</overview>

<notes>
Intro date selected as common/re-introduction date for Arrow IV field artillery
</notes>

